  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "A parabola has a turning point located at coordinates $(1,-3)$. The distance between its $x$-intercepts is $4$. Find the equation of the parabola in turning point form.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=\\frac34(x-1)^2-3$\n\nThe intercepts are $2$ units either side of the axis $x=1$.",
      "worked": "The axis of symmetry is $x=1$. The intercepts are $4$ units apart, so their $x$-coordinates are $1-2=-1$ and $1+2=3$. The turning point gives $y=A(x-1)^2-3$. Substitute $(3,0)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}0&=A(3-1)^2-3\\\\0&=4A-3\\\\A&=\\frac34\\\\y&=\\frac34(x-1)^2-3.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 54
  },
